   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Un, une, des",
     "texto": [
      "In French, all nouns are masculine or feminine. English has no gender, so learn each noun together with its article. **Un** means «a» (masculine) and **une** means «a» (feminine): **un livre**, **une clé**. In the plural, **des**: **des livres**.",
      "The definite article: **le** (the, masculine), **la** (the, feminine), **les** (the, plural). Before a vowel or a silent h, **le** and **la** become **l'**: **l'ordinateur**, **l'école**.",
      "The plural of many nouns is formed with **-s**, which is usually silent. In **le livre** / **les livres**, the difference is heard in the article."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The articles",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Masculine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Feminine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Plural",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "a (indefinite)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "un livre",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "une clé",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "des livres",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "the (definite)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "le livre",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "la clé",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "les clés",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What is this",
     "texto": [
      "**Qu'est-ce que c'est ?** = what is this?",
      "You answer with **C'est** + singular: **C'est un livre**. And **Ce sont** + plural: **Ce sont des clés**.",
      "Negative: **Ce n'est pas mon sac** (it is not my bag)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Colors",
     "texto": [
      "Unlike in English, the color adjectives in this lesson usually go after the noun and agree in gender and number: **un sac noir**, **une clé noire**, **des clés noires**.",
      "Colors that end in **-e**, like **rouge**, keep the same form in the masculine and feminine. **Blanc** has the irregular feminine **blanche**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
